0..77 Comment "// Rules whose overlap parts at a call rather than a value are completed: the"
78..156 Comment "// two rules of `swap` overlap at `swap(Zero, n)`, which one leaves at `n` and"
157..233 Comment "// the other at `add(n, Zero)`, a call the written rules cannot rewrite with"
234..310 Comment "// `n` unknown. Completion derives the rule joining the pair, `add(n, Zero)`"
311..384 Comment "// rewriting to `n`, which follows from the written rules (both sides are"
385..456 Comment "// reducts of one peak), and decides the pairs again (Knuth and Bendix,"
457..535 Comment "// _Simple Word Problems in Universal Algebras_, 1970, § 7). The kernel reads"
536..605 Comment "// the derived rule beside the written ones as one of `add`\'s (#338)."
607..680 Comment "/// The naturals with addition and an operation whose two rules part at a"
681..690 Comment "/// call."
